      <div type="clause" n="71.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 71.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ syððan cingces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.6-2"/> þegnas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.7"/>, þe hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> nyhste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.8"/> syndan: IIII hors, II<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.9"/> gesadelode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.10"/> ⁊ II unsadelode, ⁊ II<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.11"/> swurd ⁊ IIII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.12"/> spera ⁊ swa feala scylda ⁊ helm ⁊ byrnan ⁊ L<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.13"/> mances goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>Kyncges ðeines.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.1"/> And syððan kyncges ðægnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.1"/> heregeata, ðe him nyxste syndon: IIII hors, II gesadelode ⁊ twa ungesadelode, ⁊ II swyrd ⁊ IIII spera ⁊ ealswa feola scylda ⁊ helm ⁊ byrnan ⁊ fiftig mancus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.2"/> goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>And syððan cyninges þegenas, þe nihste sindon: IIII hors, twa gesadolode ⁊ twa ungesadolode ⁊ twa swurud<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/> ⁊ feower spera ⁊ swa feala scylda ⁊ helm ⁊ birnan ⁊ fiftig mancos goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Postea táini regis, qui ei proximus sit: IIII equi — duo sellati, <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.4"/>duo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.5"/> insellati<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.6"/> (non) — et duo gladii et IIII lancee et totidem scuta et galea cum lorica sua et L mancę<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.3"/> auri.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Uironis uero regis, qui est proximus ei: quatuor equi, duo cum sellis et duo sine sellis, duo gladii, quatuor lancee et totidem scuta, galea una et lorica I necnon et L mance auri.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="71a.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="210" ed="#robertson"/>Kyncges ðeines. And syððan kyncges ðægnes<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71-1.robnote.fn.1"/> heregeata<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_71-1.robnote.fn.2"/> ðe him nyxste syndon—IIII hors, II gesadelode ⁊ twa ungesadelode, ⁊ II swyrd ⁊ IIII spera ⁊ ealswa<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_71-1.robnote.fn.3"/> feola scylda ⁊ helm ⁊ byrnan ⁊ fiftig mancus goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="290" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And syððan cingces þegnas þe him nyhste syndan, IIII hors, II gesadelode and II unsadelode, and II swurd and IIII spera and swa feala scylda and helm and byrnan and L mances goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>(Eines Königsthegn. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.de.1"/> sodann (Hergewæte eines <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Königsthegnas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_71-1.lnote.de.2"/>, die ihm [dem König] zunächst stehen: 4 Pferde, 2 gesattelt und 2 ungesattelt, und 2 Schwerter und 4 Lanzen und ebenso viele Schilde und [1] Helm und Panzer und 50 Mancus [6¹/₄ Pfund] Gold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of a king's thegn. B) And then (the heriot of, B) the king's thegns who stand closest to him [the king]: 4 horses, 2 saddled and 2 unsaddled, and 2 swords and 4 spears and as many shields and [1] helmet and mail-coat and 50 mancuses [6¼ pounds] of gold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="211" ed="#robertson"/>The heriot of a king's thegn. And further, the heriots of king's thegns who stand in immediate relation to him<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71-1.robnote.n.1"/> shall be four horses, two saddled and two unsaddled, and two swords and four spears and as many shields and helmets and byrnies and 50 mancuses of gold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>and next, the king’s thegns, who are closest to him: four horses, two saddled and two unsaddled, and two swords and four spears and as many shields, and a helmet and coat of mail and 50 mancuses of gold;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="291" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And moreover, the tribute to be paid by the thanes closest to the king shall be four horses, two saddled and two unsaddled, and two swords and four spears, and just as many shields, helmets, and mail shirts, and fifty mancuses of gold.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_20-1">Leis Wl 20.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 359, October 2026 (MS Cons); AU: corrected against Rabin p. 290 / 291, October 2026 (was “iiii; iiii”, now “IIII; IIII”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Kyncges ðeines</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þegnas: B adds heregeata</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">swa: ealswa B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">spät geänd.</hi> mancusa</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">late altered to mancusa</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">fügt zu T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et added by T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">IIII <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">IIII Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so K;</hi> non <hi rend="italic">übr.;</hi> non sellati <hi rend="italic">Hk Hn</hi> 14,2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus K; non the others; non sellati Hk Hn 14,2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mancas <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mancas K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyninges <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyninges Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðegenes heregeata <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðegenes heregeata Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nihste sindon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nihste sindon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">darüber neu</hi> twa; twa <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">twa written above by a modern hand; twa Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gesadol. ⁊ twa ungesadol. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gesadol. ⁊ twa ungesadol. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">twa <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">twa Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">darüber neu</hi> feower <hi rend="italic">G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">feower written above by a modern hand G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">darüber neu</hi> fifti' <hi rend="italic">G;</hi> fiftig mancos <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fifti' written above by a modern hand G; fiftig mancos Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 14, 2 und aus Inst durch Ps Cn for 1. 6; übersetzt, mit Eigenem, durch Leis Wl 20, 1.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Thegn 5ff.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 14, 2 and, from Inst, by Ps Cn for 1. 6; translated, with additions of its own, by Leis Wl 20, 1.—<hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Thegn 5ff.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_71-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu C's <hi rend="italic">virro s. o</hi>. I 6, 2a¹; Leis Wl setzen <hi rend="italic">baron</hi>, das öfter für Königsthegn vorkommt. <hi rend="italic">Regii collaterales</hi> an Cnuts Hofe (in Hist. Ramesei. 86) hält Price hiermit identisch. Vermutlich entspricht <hi rend="italic">nyhste</hi> dem Worte <hi rend="italic">furðor cyððe</hi> der Denalagu 71, 4; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Königsdienst 4. 5. Es kann sein, dass neben jener Beziehung zum König auch, wie sicher in Denalagu, der Betrag des Grundbesitzes die Thegnklassen schied.—Hinter ‘Pfund’ ergänze, wie 71a⁸: ‘Silbers’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On C’s <hi rend="italic">virro see above</hi> I 6, 2a¹; Leis Wl put <hi rend="italic">baron</hi>, which frequently occurs for king’s thegn. Price considers the <hi rend="italic">regii collaterales</hi> at Cnut’s court (in Hist. Ramesei. 86) identical with these. Presumably <hi rend="italic">nyhste</hi> corresponds to the expression <hi rend="italic">furðor cyððe</hi> of the Danelaw, 71, 4; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Königsdienst 4. 5. It may be that, besides that relation to the king, the extent of landed property also distinguished the classes of thegn, as it certainly did in the Danelaw.—After ‘pounds’ supply, as at 71a⁸, ‘of silver’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_71-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> those whose personal lord is the king—the barons of later times, cf. Leis Wl. 20, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_71-1.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope></bibl><label>ðægnes</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þegnas</hi> G; <hi rend="italic">þegenas</hi> A.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_71-1.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope></bibl><label>heregeata</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G, A.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_71-1.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope></bibl><label>ealswa</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">swa</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
